# Non-TabPFN T06/T07 replacement implementation (2026-11-06)

## Selection evidence

Development-only aggregate AP evidence was reviewed across saved Stage 3,
Stage 4, and Stage 6 outputs. Selected models and means (sample SD):

- DEATH_BINARY: CatBoost tuned, AP 0.732590 (0.059083); strongest saved
  nonselected alternative was Random Forest tuned, 0.671321 (0.037330).
- ZSN: Random Forest tuned, AP 0.501775 (0.082878); strongest alternative
  was Extra Trees tuned, 0.485027 (0.064071).
- FIBR_PREDS: Random Forest preliminary, AP 0.301054 (0.107908), versus
  Extra Trees preliminary 0.301365 (0.125206). RF had slightly better
  development AUROC/Brier/Log Loss; the AP difference is negligible compared
  with fold variation.

Existing tuned settings differed by outer fold. The replacement freeze chooses
one existing setting using the Hamming medoid of the five saved outer-fold best
configurations; ties go to the earliest fold. Death CatBoost uses Stage 6 fold
4's setting; ZSN RF uses Stage 3 fold 4's setting. No new search is run.

## Implementation and run

- New frozen artifacts are written to `stage10_t06_non_tabpfn_outputs/`; the
  previous `stage10_t06_outputs/` is preserved.
- T06 now fits CatBoost tuned / Random Forest tuned / Random Forest preliminary
  with fresh development-only cross-fitting, Platt calibrators, and newly
  computed thresholds. No previous calibrator or threshold is loaded.
- T07 points only at the new directory and requires manifest revision
  `non_tabpfn_v1`, preventing silent fallback to the old freeze.
- Active T06/T07 no longer import TabPFN or PyTorch. There is no project
  requirements/pyproject/Pipfile/environment dependency manifest to edit;
  existing CatBoost was already present in `.venv`. Historical TabPFN scripts,
  results, and environment packages were retained for traceability.
- First approved development-only run attempt failed during input validation
  because the old TabPFN categorical-field check remained. After correcting
  the check, the next run exposed missing CatBoost `cat_features` fit metadata.
  The active pipeline was corrected to declare the same categorical columns as
  Stage 6, then the run succeeded. These attempts only read development data;
  neither accessed the held-out partition or invoked T07.

Successful command:

```text
PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 MPLCONFIGDIR=/private/tmp .venv/bin/python -B mi_stage10_t06_freeze.py --approve-development-only-run
```

The replacement output directory contains the exact 13 files declared by
`OUTPUT_FILES`. The outer OOF output contains all three targets and newly
selected threshold provenance (`pooled five-fold outer Platt OOF`); all three
thresholds meet sensitivity >= 0.80. Values: DEATH_BINARY 0.1533359551,
ZSN 0.1628645787, FIBR_PREDS 0.0710362897.

A fresh Python subprocess separately loaded each of the three bundles, predicted
on the first three `X_train.csv` rows, checked that calibrated probabilities
match the saved Platt calibrator applied to base probabilities, checked finite
[0,1] outputs, and confirmed bundle thresholds match the new threshold table.
All three passed. This check used only development rows.

