## Independent-review correction (2026-11-06)

The independent reviewer requested explicit supporting metrics for retaining
Random Forest preliminary on `FIBR_PREDS`, since Extra Trees preliminary had an
AP mean 0.000311 higher. `load_selection_evidence()` now carries development
mean AUROC, Brier, and Log Loss alongside AP, and the selection rationale in
the CSV/report/manifest explains the near tie and trade-off:

- RF: AP 0.301054 (SD 0.107908), AUROC 0.725125, Brier 0.082854, Log Loss
  0.292421.
- ET: AP 0.301365 (SD 0.125206), AUROC 0.721708, Brier 0.082892, Log Loss
  0.295108.

The AP gap is far smaller than either fold SD; RF has slightly better AUROC,
Brier, and Log Loss (lower is better). Added regression assertions for all
these rationale claims. To preserve the old T06 freeze, the corrected new
freeze was built under `.stage10_t06_non_tabpfn_rebuild/`, validated for all 13
expected files and rationale text, then atomically swapped into
`stage10_t06_non_tabpfn_outputs/`. `stage10_t06_outputs/` remained untouched.

Checks after regeneration:

- `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 MPLCONFIGDIR=/private/tmp .venv/bin/python -B -m unittest discover -s tests -v`: 45 passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed.
- Separate fresh processes loaded each regenerated bundle, checked its Platt
  mapping and new threshold, and made bounded development-row predictions:
  all three passed.
- No held-out input was accessed and T07 was not run. Independent review of
  this correction/regenerated output is pending.
